  "sectorConvention": "Indian listed general insurers are valued almost universally on one-year-forward P/E (Indian GAAP EPS), with the target set at a Sep/Mar anchor date and the multiple applied to the next fiscal year's EPS (currently FY28E). P/BV and RoE are shown only as cross-checks. Currently observed multiples: ICICI Lombard ~28-30x FY28E EPS (MOSL 28x, HSIE 29.5x Mar-28E, Emkay 30x); Star Health ~22-29x FY28E (JM 29x IGAAP = 22x Ind AS, HSIE DCF-implied 26.6x, Emkay ~22x); Go Digit ~30-35x FY28E (HSIE 31.7x, Emkay-implied ~31x, I-Sec 35x in Jun-2025). Go Digit gets a premium to ICICI Lombard because of its higher growth and lower RoE base. Departures from P/E: Emkay uses a residual-earnings/EVA model (CoE 12%) for Go Digit, and HSIE uses DCF for Star Health, but both still quote the implied FY28E P/E. With Ind AS reporting starting in FY27, brokers have begun quoting Ind AS P/E alongside IGAAP (JM on Star Health). Jefferies' convention (Aug-2024 initiation) is P/E on Sep-year-forward EPS.",
