  "notes": "Only Emkay (residual earnings/EVA) and HSIE (31.7x FY28E P/E) have a current, primary-sourced method. Jefferies 350 (TipRanks, 8-Oct-2026, cut from 380), ICICI Sec 353 (3-May-2026), Citi 405 (14-Apr-2026) and Morgan Stanley 328 (9-Apr-2026) are confirmed from Investing.com/TipRanks rating tables only, with no method found. The Investing.com dates are dd-mm-yyyy, inferred from the Jefferies date matching TipRanks. Their last known methods are all P/E on forward EPS: Jefferies 48x Sep-26 EPS at its Aug-2024 initiation, and ICICI Sec 35x FY28E EPS in Jun-2025. Treat those as indicative only. JM Financial (Buy 355) and Kotak (Neutral 330) could not be found in any public source, so their rating and TP are taken from the request and unverified; src is null. No Go Digit coverage was found for Motilal Oswal, Axis, Nuvama or HSBC. Emkay's TP date moved from Jun-27E (24-Jul-2026 note) to Sep-27E (7-Oct-2026 preview), and its implied FY28E P/E moved from 30x to ~31x. In the July note's Exhibit 2, the EVA fair value and multiples columns are garbled by PDF extraction, so treat Mar-27E fair value Rs262 and Jun-27E TP Rs270 as approximate readings. A Reuters-sourced snippet also mentions Ambit Buy 390 and Jefferies 410 (street-high, undated, likely 2025) and LSEG medians of 350-386. These were not used. Go Digit's Q2FY27 results were not out or indexed as of the search."
